# Metaphor3D — read the domain file before editing

**[`docs/agents/domains/metaphor3d.md`](../../docs/agents/domains/metaphor3d.md)**

Roughly 50 findings, each one measured from a headless render rather than reasoned about from the
code. Read its **Short form** first, then the **Full findings** entry for whatever you are about
to change.

This content used to sit in the root `CLAUDE.md` (54 KB) and `AGENTS.md` (27 KB) at once, loaded
by every session in this repo whether or not it touched a 3D scene. It is now scoped to the files
this rule globs. Same content, one copy, four agents — this rule for Cursor, a nested `CLAUDE.md`
for Claude Code, the root `AGENTS.md` index for everything else.

Two rules that catch everyone:

- **Verify by rendering, not by reading.** `apps/web/.claude/skills/verify/SKILL.md` is the
  headless-capture recipe. A visual change is not done until it has been looked at, and the
  measurement itself needs proving — a mis-captured camera once reported a clean sweep of wins the
  screenshots did not show.
- **Is this mesh the subject, or scaffolding for the subject?** Shadow catchers, ground discs,
  water planes and ambience carry `FRAME_IGNORE_DATA` so the camera does not frame them. Miss it
  and the subject renders at a fraction of the frame.

**Add findings to the domain file, once.** Do not copy them back into the root files; that
mirroring rule is retired for domain content (`docs/routines/README.md` rule 8).
